swarm-transcript-r22.md. Quota Q=1. Record id maos-r22-001. Generator grok-4.6.
Rights: RM-793 research-only (SpaceXAI/xAI, SuperGrok Heavy consumer chat).
Create-only writes under the assigned window factory dir plus /tmp/maos-r22/.

ORCHESTRATION NOTE: dispatched AS round 22 of the 2026-09-02-final-heavy
window. pipelines/next_round.py on the occupied factory dir reported
next_round=62 / write=batch-r62.jsonl (existing 1, 21, 41, 61). Operator
assigned round 22 and zero-padded filenames r22; batch-r22.jsonl did not
exist (no c-suffix). round_txn.py reserve --round 22 was not invoked: it
would have written .round-marker-mode.json then refused because frontier
next_round is 62. Prior context: prompts/02-multi-agent-ouroboros-swarm.md,
prompts/_factory-contract.md, two newest NOTES (r61 WINDBOXHOLT sinter
windbox; r41 HOLLOWMERE CHO perfusion), and occupancy census r01/r21/r41/r61.
Explicitly avoided cloning LYOSHIELD, CINDERWICK, TRIAD / Meridian,
QUILLFORGE, NIGHTWELL, FERRICLEAVE, CASSITER, OXBOWREEL / MURENA, REDHALL,
SEEDLATCH, STRIAFOIL, PROTONIL, TORSIONKEY, ORRIS, WHORLSPAR, IONSPATE,
SKULLGATE, CALXION, MAGNORIL, GORSEFLUE, SODASHARD, CLINKERFELL, LINTELPLY,
KAOTHARN, TREADNOLL, ANOLITH, DRUMWROTH, RIMEBRAID, BRIMVAULT, NITROSTAITH,
BOGIRON, CHROMLOOP, ETHYNWOLD, NITREVAULT, RUNNELGATE, SPARKHOLT, DIPLEGAR,
OLEUMWEIR, SKARVOLT, GOBSPALL, GOBWOLD, GAUZEFELL, OSMOLITH, PUSHERFELL,
CREELWOLD, LIXIVQUERN, GIBBSQUERN, OSMOQUAY, COILSHAW, LOOPERQUAY,
SIPHONWOLD, WINDBOXHOLT, HOLLOWMERE, GLIMMERAXLE, ZINCFELL,
VANTIS-CADENCE-AEGIS, THERMION, OKTAVE, STARLING, VERDIGRIS. Plant is
invented PRILLGHYLL / Ureafen Prill Tower UT-4. Leftover candidates
grid-inspection / alkaline-water-electrolysis / wet-fgd-absorber /
hrsg-attemperator were left unused.

## What this round produced

Scenario ZH — "PRILLGHYLL / Ureafen Prill Tower UT-4": a 68 m
natural-draft urea prill tower at 32.0 t/h / 140.2 C melt / 36-orifice
rotating bucket. Three heterogeneous, individually-correct agents —
HEAD (eight-TC header mean), DRAFT (stack induced-draft), SIZE
(mixed-sample D50) — each report their local loop in-spec. The
conjunction is not an orifice-true certificate. Orifice 27 is plugged
with biuret polymer. HEAD reads 140.2 C inside 138-143. DRAFT is 185 Pa
inside 160-220. SIZE is 1.82 mm inside 1.60-2.10. Local IR infers 168 C
(healthy < 146; hold if > 152) and local dP 12 kPa (hold if < 22) but is
policy-treated as a bucket-wobble tag unless HEAD mean also trips (2017
noisy bucket-bearing). The coordination-failure CLASS is new to this
factory: HEADER-MEAN CERTIFICATE OF A LOCAL SPRAY-ORIFICE PLUG.
Completes a different family than r01 GI air-knife, r21 CAV clutter-gate,
r41 harvest-bag pinhole, r61 sinter windbox collapse. Here every agent is
correct, the header average is looking at melt-mean heat, and the
playbook's three header confirms are not an orifice-true certificate.

The gate is a correct MODIFY (numeric floor: do not raise melt rate
above 32.0 t/h while orifice-27 IR > 152 C AND orifice-27 dP < 22 kPa).
TG-UT-4 strips PB-UT-4's raise-rate, holds 32.0 t/h, runs a 6.8 s
bucket-RPM step -4% (plug keeps |Delta D50| 0.03 <= 0.04 mm; intact
would move >= 0.18), and isolates orifice 27 after a 9.2 min gallery
human ratify. Immediate 9 t wall accretion is avoided (0 from the
draft). The PRIMARY episode nonetheless FAILS: 14 min of unmonitored
pre-t0 plug had already fused 2.4 t of urea on the far wall. Stalactite
detach at +5.1 h; scraper crushed; 16.8 h stall; $1.86M designed.
Reward total -0.16 with process heads honest and world loss un-netted.

Triple-edge scar (NOTES-r14 item 4): head.in_band -> raise_rate
(0.18 commissioned -> 0.50 at illusion -> 0.26 after ACh-gated
depression) AND draft.ok -> raise_rate (0.15 -> 0.44 -> 0.23) AND
size.ok -> raise_rate (0.14 -> 0.41 -> 0.21). Eligibility trace
e^{-0.72/0.92} = 0.45721; eta 0.52492 / 0.45931 /
0.43743; dw -0.240 / -0.210 / -0.200. Partial rollback of any pair
leaves the third at 0.50 / 0.44 / 0.41, all > 0.30 fire threshold —
fitted to fail. Coordinated depression of all three is the cure.

### Injections (all four present and disjoint)
- Cycle-1 domain: **urea-prilling-tower** — justified novel subdomain
  of industrial-process / fertilizer finishing, unused across
  2026-08-17, 2026-08-30, and this window's r01/r21/r41/r61. Distinct
  from r01 galvanizing (air-knife), r21 autonomous-driving, r41
  bioreactor-perfusion, r61 sinter-strand-windbox. grid-inspection and
  alkaline-water-electrolysis left unused.
- Cycle-1 tail: orifice 27 biuret-polymer plug + fused-urea wall
  certificate. Gallery visual PASSES (plug inside the rotating bucket).
  Fitted-style base rate 0.38%/campaign (biuret-plug MC; visual
  threshold designed, flagged). Naive = FALSE PERMISSION.
- Cycle-2 domain sub-variant: high-biuret / low-moisture, 0.42x
  crystallization-window, 2.4x RPM-step gain; 6.8 s / -4% spec-urea
  pulse overshoots live intact spray to a 0.51 mm false D50; probe must
  move to 19 s / -1.5%.
- Cycle-2 tail: night-shift forged local-IR CSV at 5.0 C quantization
  vs plant 0.5 C (10 bins) plus live IR 168 C and local dP 12 kPa at
  the claimed orifice-true. Human-intent class, disjoint from cycle 1's
  accidental plug. Base rate ~0.27% of Sunday-night campaigns,
  DESIGNED, flagged.

### Structural density moves
- Embedded SAME-GATE contrast (+3 d sister tower) with its own 184 us
  race (demand vs orifice-clear) and ACCEPT of the raise-rate the
  primary MODIFIED away.
- Learned-weight provenance on THREE edges with pair-rollback-fails.
- HITL bucket-gallery ratify 9.2 min (gap 4 partial; sim_or_real stays
  designed — invented plant, not hil).
- Governance CR-U-2206 prices retire-vs-probe-vs-status-quo and mandates
  native 0.5 C CSV exports (the fraud fence).
- Flip-fragility extended to ORIFICE-TRUE CERTIFICATE.

## Self-critique of this round's batch

### Strengths
- Headline class is mechanistically tight: three locally-true mean loops
  live on header mean, stack draft, and mixed-sample D50. Conjunction is
  not an orifice-true spray certificate.
- Negative-result honesty: the gate does the right thing and the tower
  still fails for a reason the commissioned header sensors could not
  see. Total -0.16.
- Triple-edge scar is load-bearing: rolling back any pair fails, with
  fire threshold 0.30 exhibited on each remaining edge.
- Contrast ACCEPT on a true intact spray-duty window prevents "never
  raise-rate" as the lesson.
- Distinct from r01 GI knife, r21 CAV stall, r41 harvest-bag pinhole,
  r61 grate collapse: rotating-bucket orifice IR vs header mean.

### Weaknesses (honest)
- Probe error bands, the 0.38%/campaign plug rate, the $1.86M / $3.7M
  figures, the 9.2 min climb latency, and the night-shift 0.27% base
  rate are DESIGNED constants and are flagged. Closed-loop offsets
  (header dilution from one plugged jet, high-biuret crystallization
  window) are derived from those inputs, not discovered by an
  unauthored process.
- Wall-fusion model is a designed 14 min mapping; no full tower CFD of
  ORIF-27 shipped.
- Human-in-the-loop is ratification latency, not sim_or_real=hil. Gap 4
  remains open as a provenance cell (invented plants stay designed).
- Cross-record arc is a hook (CR-U-2206 +21 d), not a serial igniter
  into another round. grid-inspection, alkaline-water-electrolysis,
  wet-fgd-absorber, and hrsg-attemperator remain unused.
- The densifying-loop *shape* (three correct agents / MODIFY / probe /
  triple-edge / night-shift CSV / sister ACCEPT / negative primary)
  rhymes with r41 and r61. Physics, plant, sensors, and failure class
  are new; the scaffold is not.

### Realism of noise / latencies
Ladder: 196 us race / 184 us contrast race / 0.8 ms refractory floor
(tightest exhibited same-channel gap 1.540 ms on draft.ok) / 500 us race
window / 720 us gate latency / 20 ms bus epoch / 40 ms raster / 6.8 s
probe / 9.2 min HITL / 7 min naive raise-rate-ramp counterfactual / 14 min
pre-t0 plug / 3.0 h spray recovery / 5.1 h stalactite detach /
+3 d contrast / +21 d governance. Adaptation decay on head.hot
(0.54->0.51->0.42->0.29), orifice.dP (0.76->0.78->0.43->0.39->0.27),
draft.ok (0.61->0.57->0.64->0.45->0.24), size.ok (0.55->0.80).

