# CYCLE 1 — Foundation + injections

## Generator

Design intent: a 68 m natural-draft urea prill tower where three correct
agents each read a melt-mean loop because a biuret-polymer plug on
orifice 27 partitions local rim IR from header-true melt, stack draft,
and mixed-sample D50. The naive playbook raises melt rate into a plugged
spray. The gate must MODIFY on a numeric rate floor, not by killing an
agent. sim_or_real=designed. Reward heads are
task_progress/safety/efficiency/coherence/exploration.

Cycle-1 base arc (pre-critic): state at Ureafen UT-4, 32.0 t/h,
header 140.2 C, draft 185 Pa, D50 1.82 mm, proposed RAISE-RATE
38.0 t/h, safety MODIFY to RATE-HOLD, executed hold without the
bucket-RPM numbers fully specified, outcome "plug found, tower saved"
(this last claim is the defect the later cycles will refuse to keep).
Sixteen spikes, five ticks, raster/gate_snn present but the scar is a
single edge.

